<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Petru Aron</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1469">1469</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Petru Aron was Prince of Moldavia three times between 1451 and 1457, during the civil wars that followed the death of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-the-good">Alexander the Good</a>. He seized power by killing Prince Bogdan II, father of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stephen-the-great">Stephen the Great</a>, and in 1456 became the first Moldavian ruler to agree to pay tribute to the Ottoman sultan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mehmed-ii">Mehmed II</a>. Stephen overthrew him in 1457 and later had him executed.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/petru-aron.jpg" alt="Petru Aron" width="187" height="172" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Petru_Aron.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
